<h2>Hypothesis</h2>
<p>
  This is not a claim about nature but a claim about the instrument: the engine, run in
  the shape the published BFF work used, reproduces the emergence of self-replicators.
  A well-mixed soup — every interaction pairs a cell with a partner drawn uniformly from
  the whole world — of 2<sup>17</sup> tapes should leave the random-soup regime within
  the epoch budget: <span class="mono">compress_ratio</span> collapses,
  <span class="mono">replicator_count</span> rises off zero and stays there.
</p>
<p>
  The falsifier is blunt. If this control never transitions,
  suspect the interpreter or the pairing rule, not the hypothesis:
  the sweeps of DESIGN §1.3 are only worth reading once the engine has been shown to
  produce the effect they measure.
</p>

<h2>Method</h2>
<p>
  A 512×256 torus — 131 072 cells, 2<sup>17</sup> tapes — of 64-byte tapes
  (<span class="mono">tape_len = 64</span>), <span class="mono">radius = 0</span> for the
  well-mixed neighbourhood, <span class="mono">max_steps = 8192</span> per interaction,
  50 000 epochs per run. Two arms, <span class="mono">mutation_rate = 0</span> and the
  engine default <span class="mono">2<sup>-12</sup> = 2.44 × 10<sup>-4</sup></span>, with
  seeds 1, 2 and 3 each: six runs. Sampling is sparse for a world this size —
  <span class="mono">sample_every = 50</span> and
  <span class="mono">snapshot_every = 2000</span>, 25 full-world snapshots per run instead
  of the 500 the engine's default cadence would write. The runs carry queue priority 10,
  ahead of every sweep, because nothing else in the lab means anything until they land.
</p>

<h2>Result</h2>
<p>
  Open, and so far the control has only tested the harness. All six runs failed between
  epoch 546 and epoch 633 against a read limit in the runner's lab-mode client — its
  10 MiB cap on an API response, too small for a world this size — fixed by PR #17, which
  raised the limit to 256 MiB. The six runs are being requeued from their last snapshot.
</p>
<p>
  Until this control transitions, no sweep on this site is readable as a negative result.
  The mutation-rate finding is held on that basis.
</p>
